# Sketch alignment and distribution candidate

This frozen work-only candidate adds six alignment actions and horizontal/vertical distribution. All28 focused implementation/DOM/persistence checks pass, with zero skips and53 source files exact before/after. A source-assisted comparison covers1,944 scene/action pairs from3 authored fixtures and240 seeded scenes; it is one author corpus, without independent held-out or full-original GUI acceptance.

Exact pinned source at Excalidraw0.18.1 commit a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84 includes MIT attribution. Seven complete source slices from five units are TypeScript-stripped into one verification VM: alignment/translation, distribution, maximum groups, common bounds/box, and both mutation helpers. Owned unrotated geometry extrema, unbound-text, no-opbinding, timestamp/random/scene/elbow dependency adapters are explicit. Original renderer, frame/binding maintenance and whole application are not executed.

Three preceding27/28 runs remain exact. The first discovered an owned unconditional mutation adapter that incorrectly converted negative zero; replacing it with both complete original mutation helpers left the candidate unchanged. The next confirmed a candidate distribution negative-zero difference when original newElementWith copied both coordinate arithmetic results. The third confirmed last-bit distribution differences from combining gap+extent additions. Candidate corrections preserve exact original conditional copy and sequential addition; numeric assertions use no tolerance/rounding normalization. A missing14th baseline storage snapshot was restored from byte-authenticated unchanged current storage; the preparation fault is retained.

Imported mixed opaque groups and externally bound containers refuse layout; this is narrower than complete native layout. Groups expand to their editable outer members, retaining internal offsets, selection and one-step Undo/Redo. Existing signed/freehand geometry, native unknown metadata, saved scene roundtrips and active gesture refusal are tested. Actual current browser use, independent review, installation, original GUI and quality comparisons remain pending. Production stays untouched.
